# Frontend Development & Modern Fluid Responsive Standards (European High Standard)

## 1. Environment & Units (WCAG & Accessibility Standards)
- Operate in SCSS mode using `src/scss/`.
- Maintain browser default root font size (`html { font-size: 100%; }` / 16px). Forcing `62.5%` or arbitrary root scaling is strictly prohibited.
- Convert px to rem using the `rem($px)` function in `src/scss/_mixins.scss` (e.g., `rem(24)` -> `1.5rem`).
- Utilize standard CSS `clamp()` or fluid functions for scalable typography and dynamic spacing.
- Prioritize design tokens defined in `:root` (`var(--color-*)`) for colors, spacing, and base fonts. Hardcoded values are strictly forbidden.

## 2. Fluid Design & Robust Responsiveness (Zero Horizontal Overflow)
- **Seamless Fluid Tracking (No Horizontal Scroll):**
  Ensure strictly zero horizontal scrolling across all viewport widths from 375px (mobile) to 4K (desktop).
- **Prohibition of Rigid Fixed Pixel Widths:**
  Avoid fixed widths (e.g., `width: 500px`) on layout containers. Use `max-width: 100%`, flexbox wrapping, or CSS Grid with `minmax(0, 1fr)`.
- **Large-screen Restraints (Figma Max-width Constraints):**
  Apply explicit maximum widths defined in Figma (e.g., `max-width: rem(688)`) to prevent unbounded expansion. Avoid `flex-grow: 1; max-width: none;` on wide displays.
- **Autonomous Tablet Optimization (769px - 1023px):**
  Even without dedicated tablet mockups in Figma, dynamically prevent cramped layouts by scaling down gaps/paddings or gracefully wrapping columns (e.g., 2x2 grid) to preserve visual hierarchy.

## 3. Media Strategy & Performance Optimization (Retina, WebP, Core Web Vitals)
- **Asset Extraction via Figma MCP:**
  Export raster images (photos/illustrations) in high resolution (Retina 2x scale: 2) as PNG/JPG, and convert to optimized `.webp` placed in `src/assets/images/`.
- **Next-Gen Responsive Delivery via picture Tag:**
  Wrap critical raster images in semantic `<picture>` tags supporting WebP (1x/2x) with proper fallbacks (PNG/JPG 1x/2x):
  - Example: Provide `<source type="image/webp" srcset="image.webp 1x, image@2x.webp 2x">` with a fallback `<img>`.
- **Performance Attributes Strategy:**
  - Above-the-fold (Hero section): `loading="lazy"` is STRICTLY PROHIBITED. Apply `fetchpriority="high"` to optimize LCP.
  - Below-the-fold (Portfolio section): `loading="lazy"` and `decoding="async"` are MANDATORY to reduce initial payload and eliminate scroll jank.
- **CLS (Cumulative Layout Shift) Prevention:**
  Always specify explicit `width` and `height` attributes or CSS `aspect-ratio` on all images to reserve layout space prior to asset load. Meaningful, descriptive `alt` text is required for all informative images.

## 4. Typography & Word Wrap Protection
- **Short UI Text Protection:**
  Apply `white-space: nowrap;` to short interface elements such as navigation links, footer links, tags, and CTA buttons.
- **Strict Prohibition of Broken Words:**
  Prevent mid-word breaks or orphan characters (e.g., "Condition\ns"). If space is constrained, drop the entire block gracefully rather than truncating typography.

## 5. Grid Architecture (Equal Pitch Columns)
- For multi-column groups (e.g., navigation columns, card grids), enforce equal-width grids (e.g., `repeat(N, 1fr)`) to maintain consistent heading start alignment regardless of content character length.

## 6. Semantic HTML & Accessibility (a11y / WCAG 2.1 AA)
- Strictly follow BEM naming conventions (Block__Element--Modifier). Avoid nesting deeper than 3 levels in SCSS.
- Use native HTML5 landmarks (`header`, `main`, `section`, `nav`, `footer`, `small`, `article`, `figure`) and avoid unsemantic `div` soup.
- Screen Reader Support: Interactive icon-only controls must include `aria-label` or visually-hidden labels (`.visually-hidden`).
- Keyboard Navigation: All interactive elements must provide visible, accessible `:focus-visible` outlines in addition to `:hover` states.

## 7. Quality Assurance
- Ensure `npm run build` passes with zero errors before finalizing code outputs.